{"slug":"sql-between","wpId":470,"title":"MySQL Between","category":"sql","categories":["sql"],"tags":[],"date":"2019-03-31T08:29:41","modified":"2021-01-19T01:31:03","excerpt":"The BETWEEN is used in the WHERE clause to check if a value is in a range. Here is an example of BETWEEN and AND. We are querying customers that have sales rep with id between 1 and 7. BETWEEN can also be done by using >= and <=. Here is an example of […]","url":"/sql/sql-between","contentHtml":"<div class=\"boldgrid-section\">\n<div class=\"container\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12 col-sm-12\">\n<p> </p>\n<p>The BETWEEN is used in the WHERE clause to check if a value is in a range.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<p class=\"mod-reset\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-768\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2019/04/image-40.png\"/></p>\n</figure>\n<div class=\"boldgrid-section\">\n<div class=\"container\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12 col-sm-12\">\n<p>Here is an example of BETWEEN and AND. We are querying customers that have sales rep with id between 1 and 7.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<p class=\"mod-reset\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-770\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2019/04/image-41.png\"/></p>\n</figure>\n<div class=\"boldgrid-section\">\n<div class=\"container\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12 col-sm-12\">\n<p>BETWEEN can also be done by using &gt;= and &lt;=.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<p class=\"mod-reset\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-771\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2019/04/image-42.png\"/></p>\n</figure>\n<div class=\"boldgrid-section\">\n<div class=\"container\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12 col-sm-12\">\n<p>Here is an example of BETWEEN with NOT</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<p class=\"mod-reset\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-772\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2019/04/image-43.png\"/></p>\n</figure>\n<div class=\"boldgrid-section\">\n<div class=\"container\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12 col-sm-12\">\n<p><strong>BETWEEN with Date comparison</strong></p>\n<p>It is best practice to convert the value to the DATE datatype before using it with the BETWEEN clause.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<p class=\"mod-reset\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-774\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2019/04/image-44.png\"/></p>\n</figure>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<p class=\"mod-reset\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-775\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://d2q2snz6diubfd.cloudfront.net/media/2019/04/image-45.png\"/></p>\n</figure>\n<div class=\"boldgrid-section\">\n<div class=\"container\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12 col-sm-12\">\n<p> </p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>","toc":[],"wordCount":80,"readingMinutes":1,"status":"published"}